  "description": "Some days speed and efficiency are king, and we need to get to the finish line - fast. Other days, gravel roads beckon us to explore off the beaten path. With its split personality - both race-oriented and self-sufficient - the Buzzard is ready for it all. Our versatile carbon gravel bike has a long front triangle for stability and a short rear end with flared chain stays that make it easy to whip through tight singletrack. In-frame downtube storage and 18 mounts accommodate racks, fenders and panniers for multi-day adventure rides. Internal cable routing, UDH compatibility and space for wide tires (up to a 45c in the rear) make the Buzzard sleek and functional. Whether it's a quick gravel grind, a destination race, or an epic bikepacking adventure, the Buzzard will take you on roads less traveled.\nThe Buzzard 1 has the same stiff carbon frame and fork, with a Rival AXS groupset with double chainring for more versatility and climbing range for when the terrain tops out. Coupled with FSA SL-K AGX tubeless carbon wheels and Vittoria Terreno Dry gravel tires, this Buzzard will slay even the steepest dirt climbs.",
